    text "e278" {
        x: 206;
        y: 632;
        width: 880;
        height: 170;
        content: "Let $s \\in \\partial R(\\Omega)$. By (1), $s \\in R(F_0)$ for $F_0$ exposed; while $s \\in \\partial R(F_k)$, (2) moves the root to $R(F_{k+1})$ for $F_{k+1} \\subsetneq F_k$ exposed, so $\\dim F_{k+1} < \\dim F_k$. The dimension drops strictly at each step, hence the process terminates at an exposed edge $E$ with $s \\in R(E)$.";
        fontSize: 21;
        lineHeight: 1.45;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a211";
