    text "e305" {
        x: 156;
        y: 352;
        width: 1600;
        height: 120;
        content: "Proof. $s \\in R(\\Omega)$ gives $\\delta \\in \\Omega$ with $\\tilde{P}_\\delta(s) = 0$. Since $\\mathrm{Im}(s) = 0$ we have $s = \\bar{r}$ with $r = \\mathrm{Re}(s)$. The root at $\\bar{r}$ reads $P_\\delta(r) = 0$, i.e. $\\delta \\in \\ker(\\mathrm{ev}_r) = P_{s_r}(r)$.";
        fontSize: 22;
        lineHeight: 1.5;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
