slide "Edge Theorem — formal proof" {
    id: "s60";
    background: "#ffffff";

    text "e637" {
        x: 120;
        y: 44;
        width: 1680;
        height: 64;
        content: "Edge Theorem — formal proof";
        fontSize: 44;
        fontWeight: 700;
        color: "#12233a";
    }

    rect "e638" {
        x: 120;
        y: 124;
        width: 120;
        height: 6;
        fill: "#1f4e79";
        radius: 3;
    }

    rect "e639" {
        x: 120;
        y: 168;
        width: 1680;
        height: 96;
        fill: "#f2f6fa";
        radius: 8;
        animate {
            id: "a492";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    rect "e640" {
        x: 120;
        y: 168;
        width: 8;
        height: 96;
        fill: "#1f4e79";
        radius: 4;
        animate {
            id: "a493";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e641" {
        x: 148;
        y: 181;
        width: 1620;
        height: 74;
        content: "Theorem (Edge Theorem). Let $\\Omega \\subset \\mathbb{R}^{n+1}$ ($n \\ge 1$) be a polytope satisfying Assumption 6.1. Then every\n$s \\in \\partial R(\\Omega)$ lies in $R(E)$ for some exposed edge $E$ of $\\Omega$.";
        fontSize: 19;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a494";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e642" {
        x: 120;
        y: 286;
        width: 820;
        height: 30;
        content: "Proof";
        fontSize: 20;
        fontWeight: 700;
        color: "#5c6878";
        animate {
            id: "a495";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e643" {
        x: 120;
        y: 352;
        width: 820;
        height: 74;
        content: "1. Let $s \\in \\partial R(\\Omega)$. Since $R(\\Omega)$ is closed,\n$s \\in R(\\Omega)$ and $s \\notin \\mathrm{int}\\,R(\\Omega)$.";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a496";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e644" {
        x: 120;
        y: 451;
        width: 820;
        height: 74;
        content: "2. If $\\mathrm{Im}(s) = 0$, Lemma 6.1 (real case) gives an\nexposed edge $E$ with $s \\in R(E)$. Done.";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a497";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e645" {
        x: 120;
        y: 550;
        width: 820;
        height: 105;
        content: "3. Else $\\mathrm{Im}(s) \\ne 0$: Lemma 6.1 (complex case) gives an\nexposed face $F$ with $s \\in R(F)$ and\n$\\dim\\mathrm{aff}(F) \\le 2$.";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a498";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e646" {
        x: 120;
        y: 681;
        width: 820;
        height: 201;
        content: "4. If $\\dim = 2$: $R(F)$ is closed, and\n$\\mathrm{int}\\,R(F) \\subseteq \\mathrm{int}\\,R(\\Omega) \\not\\ni s$,\nso $s \\in \\partial R(F)$. Lemma 6.2 moves $s$ to\n$R(\\mathrm{relativeBoundary}\\,F)$; the witness lies on the\nrelative boundary, giving a proper exposed subface\n$G \\subsetneq F$ ($\\dim G \\le 1$) with $s \\in R(G)$.";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a499";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e647" {
        x: 120;
        y: 907;
        width: 820;
        height: 137;
        content: "5. If $\\dim \\le 1$: the face ($G$, resp. $F$) is already an edge\n($\\dim = 1$) or a singleton ($\\dim = 0$), and a singleton face\nsits on an exposed edge through it. Either way $s \\in R(E)$ for\nan exposed edge $E$. ∎";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a500";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e648" {
        x: 980;
        y: 286;
        width: 820;
        height: 30;
        content: "Lean (EdgeTheorem.lean)";
        fontSize: 20;
        fontWeight: 700;
        color: "#5c6878";
        animate {
            id: "a501";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e649" {
        x: 980;
        y: 368;
        width: 820;
        height: 67;
        content: "Closedness + unpacking: rootSpaceSet_isClosed_of_isCompact,\nfrontier_subset_closure.";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a502";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e650" {
        x: 980;
        y: 477;
        width: 820;
        height: 38;
        content: "Step 2 is edge_real (exactly lemma61_real).";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a503";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e651" {
        x: 980;
        y: 558;
        width: 820;
        height: 67;
        content: "Step 3 is lemma61_complex_with_dim (face of dimension at most\ntwo).";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a504";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e652" {
        x: 980;
        y: 666;
        width: 820;
        height: 74;
        content: "Step 4 uses interior_mono with $R(F) \\subseteq R(\\Omega)$ to land\nin $\\partial R(F)$; Lemma 6.2 enters as face_boundary_subset.";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a505";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e653" {
        x: 980;
        y: 782;
        width: 820;
        height: 152;
        content: "The last descent is exists_proper_subface_of_boundary_point,\nclosing via isExposedEdge_of_dim_1 or\nexposed_face_dim_zero_singleton +\nexists_exposed_edge_of_singleton (factored as\nexposed_face_root_dim_le1_to_edge).";
        fontSize: 20;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a506";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e654" {
        x: 980;
