    code "e659" {
        x: 120;
        y: 250;
        width: 1680;
        height: 97;
        content: "lemma rootSpaceSet_isClosed_of_isCompact {n : ℕ} {W : Set (CoeffVec n)} (hW : IsCompact W) :\n    IsClosed (RootSpaceSet W)";
        language: "lean";
        theme: "light";
        fontSize: 16;
        animate {
            id: "a510";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e660" {
        x: 120;
        y: 368;
        width: 1680;
        height: 91;
        content: "How: Let $Z = \\{(\\delta, s) \\in W \\times \\mathbb{C} : \\tilde P_\\delta(s) = 0\\}$, the set of polynomial–root pairs. It is closed, being the zero set of the\ncontinuous evaluation map. $\\pi(\\delta, s) = s$ satisfies $\\pi(Z) = R(W)$: indeed $s \\in \\pi(Z)$ iff some $\\delta \\in W$ vanishes at $s$. Since $W$ is\ncompact, $\\pi : W \\times \\mathbb{C} \\to \\mathbb{C}$ is a closed map, so $\\pi(Z) = R(W)$ is closed.";
        fontSize: 17;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a511";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e661" {
        x: 120;
        y: 479;
        width: 1680;
        height: 34;
        content: "Step 2. Every real root of the family already lives on an exposed edge.";
        fontSize: 17;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a512";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e662" {
        x: 120;
        y: 533;
        width: 1680;
        height: 21;
        content: "EdgeTheorem.lean:37-40";
        fontSize: 15.2;
        color: "#5c6878";
        animate {
            id: "a513";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    code "e663" {
        x: 120;
        y: 561;
        width: 1680;
        height: 121;
        content: "theorem edge_real {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≥ 1) (P : Polytope n) (s : ℂ)\n    (hs : s ∈ RootSpace P) (hreal : s.im = 0) :\n    ∃ E, IsExposedEdge P E ∧ s ∈ RootSpaceSet E";
        language: "lean";
        theme: "light";
        fontSize: 16;
        animate {
            id: "a514";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e664" {
        x: 120;
        y: 702;
        width: 1680;
        height: 37;
        content: "How: Lemma 6.1, real case: $s = \\bar{r} \\in R(\\Omega)$ yields $E$ with $s \\in R(E)$.";
        fontSize: 17;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a515";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
            duration: 320;
            delay: 0;
            easing: "easeOut";
            direction: "up";
            repeat: 1;
        }
    }

    text "e665" {
        x: 120;
        y: 759;
        width: 1680;
        height: 34;
        content: "Step 3. Every non-real root lives on an exposed face of dimension at most two.";
        fontSize: 17;
        lineHeight: 1.42;
        color: "#24313f";
        math: true;
        animate {
            id: "a516";
            effect: "fadeIn";
            trigger: "onClick";
